glmark2-mali-tally: causes of new (main `099b5df6`): 1

## Draft issue 1

Title: gpu-mali: glmark2-es2 terrain on the NanoPC-T6: gpu-fault: panthor fb000000.gpu: [drm] *ERROR* Unhandled Page fault in AS3 at VA <hex>

Cause 1: gpu-fault: panthor fb000000.gpu: [drm] *ERROR* Unhandled Page fault in AS3 at VA <hex>

The first glmark2-es2 run on the NanoPC-T6 (Mali-G610, panthor, back end gpu-mali, #20) from main `099b5df6` (kernel 6.18.55-current-rockchip64, the tools/mali/panthor-gles pair, libGLESv2.so.2 sha256 `3f6c0a1d9e2b4c5a`), one glmark2-es2 process per scene at 800x600 on an EGL pbuffer, gives verdict gpu-fault in 1 scene(s): `[terrain] <default>`.

- `[terrain] <default>`: exit 0, timeout 0, panthor kernel lines 3; 333.33 ms a frame
  > yakogl-mali-exit: draws=40 refused=0 first_refused=- gpu_faults=1 job_timeouts=0
  > kmsg: panthor fb000000.gpu: [drm] *ERROR* Unhandled Page fault in AS3 at VA 0x0000000100004000

Run directory `new`, tallied by `tools/cts/glmark2-mali-tally.py`. Rerun the scene alone with tools/cts/mali-glmark2-run.sh to reproduce. ROADMAP.md stage 2 asks for all 33 scenes with no failed scene, no GL error and no scene out of GPU memory.

